{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFTzhVMxPCuXLj9XqyjcVc","type":"tool_result","content":"398\t<!-- FIGURE: ch12-fig02-rbac-four-way-matrix -->\n399\t```\n400\t   THE BOUNDARY YOU ALREADY HAVE  (Ch 4 §3)\n401\t   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n402\t\n403\t   NAMESPACED resource                       CLUSTER-SCOPED resource\n404\t   lives inside a namespace                  lives in NO namespace\n405\t   Pod, Service, Secret,                     Node, PersistentVolume,\n406\t   Deployment, ConfigMap                     StorageClass, Namespace\n407\t        │                                            │\n408\t        │                                            │\n409\t        │  a Role's scope has room for it            │  a Role has nowhere\n410\t        │                                            │  to put it\n411\t        ▼                                            ▼\n412\t   ┌─────────────────────┐                  ┌─────────────────────┐\n413\t   │ Role                │                  │ ClusterRole         │\n414\t   │  or ClusterRole     │  ◀── either ──   │  FORCED             │\n415\t   └─────────────────────┘                  └─────────────────────┘\n416\t\n417\t\n418\t   THE SECOND, INDEPENDENT QUESTION\n419\t   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n420\t\n421\t        where should the grant apply?\n422\t                  │\n423\t        ┌─────────┴──────────┐\n424\t        ▼                    ▼\n425\t   one namespace        every namespace\n426\t        │                    │\n427\t        ▼                    ▼\n428\t   ┌──────────────┐    ┌─────────────────────┐\n429\t   │ RoleBinding  │    │ ClusterRoleBinding  │\n430\t   └──────────────┘    └─────────────────────┘\n431\t\n432\t\n433\t   THE FOUR COMBINATIONS FALL OUT\n434\t   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n435\t\n436\t   Role      + RoleBinding         → those rules, in that namespace\n437\t   ClusterRole + RoleBinding       → those rules, in that ONE namespace\n438\t   ClusterRole + ClusterRoleBinding→ those rules, everywhere\n439\t   Role      + ClusterRoleBinding  → ✗ does not exist. A Role's rules\n440\t                                       are namespace-local; there is\n441\t                                       nothing cluster-wide to grant.\n442\t\n443\t   ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n444\t   │  ▶  THE BINDING DETERMINES THE SCOPE OF THE GRANT.            │\n445\t   └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n446\t```\n447\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7de6482-238e-46bc-bfd1-6b5d0d0774fe","uuid":"8ff843ff-ae1d-44de-96cc-2217006e2ed2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:23:56.898Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-12\\draft-v1.md","content":"<!-- FIGURE: ch12-fig02-rbac-four-way-matrix -->\n```\n   THE BOUNDARY YOU ALREADY HAVE  (Ch 4 §3)\n   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n\n   NAMESPACED resource                       CLUSTER-SCOPED resource\n   lives inside a namespace                  lives in NO namespace\n   Pod, Service, Secret,                     Node, PersistentVolume,\n   Deployment, ConfigMap                     StorageClass, Namespace\n        │                                            │\n        │                                            │\n        │  a Role's scope has room for it            │  a Role has nowhere\n        │                                            │  to put it\n        ▼                                            ▼\n   ┌─────────────────────┐                  ┌─────────────────────┐\n   │ Role                │                  │ ClusterRole         │\n   │  or ClusterRole     │  ◀── either ──   │  FORCED             │\n   └─────────────────────┘                  └─────────────────────┘\n\n\n   THE SECOND, INDEPENDENT QUESTION\n   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n\n        where should the grant apply?\n                  │\n        ┌─────────┴──────────┐\n        ▼                    ▼\n   one namespace        every namespace\n        │                    │\n        ▼                    ▼\n   ┌──────────────┐    ┌─────────────────────┐\n   │ RoleBinding  │    │ ClusterRoleBinding  │\n   └──────────────┘    └─────────────────────┘\n\n\n   THE FOUR COMBINATIONS FALL OUT\n   ─────────────────────────────────────────\n\n   Role      + RoleBinding         → those rules, in that namespace\n   ClusterRole + RoleBinding       → those rules, in that ONE namespace\n   ClusterRole + ClusterRoleBinding→ those rules, everywhere\n   Role      + ClusterRoleBinding  → ✗ does not exist. A Role's rules\n                                       are namespace-local; there is\n                                       nothing cluster-wide to grant.\n\n   ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │  ▶  THE BINDING DETERMINES THE SCOPE OF THE GRANT.            │\n   └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n","numLines":50,"startLine":398,"totalLines":1764}}}
