{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011QnBwUSsAe8VfErJUfhZn7","type":"tool_result","content":"876\t<!-- FIGURE: ch12-fig04-pod-security-standards-levels -->\n877\t```\n878\t   THE LEVELS — what gets checked\n879\t   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n880\t\n881\t   securityContext field          privileged   baseline    restricted\n882\t   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n883\t   privileged: true               allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n884\t   hostNetwork/hostPID/hostIPC    allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n885\t   hostPath volumes               allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n886\t   hostPort                       allowed      restricted  restricted\n887\t   capabilities.add               allowed      known list  only\n888\t                                                           NET_BIND_SERVICE\n889\t   capabilities.drop              —            —           must include ALL\n890\t   seccompProfile.type            allowed      not          RuntimeDefault\n891\t                                               Unconfined   or Localhost\n892\t   appArmorProfile.type           allowed      Runtime      Runtime\n893\t                                               Default or   Default or\n894\t                                               Localhost    Localhost\n895\t   allowPrivilegeEscalation       allowed      —           must be false\n896\t   runAsNonRoot                   —            —           must be true\n897\t   runAsUser                      any          any         must be non-zero\n898\t                                                           or unset\n899\t   volume types                   any          any         safe list only\n900\t                                                           (configMap, csi,\n901\t                                                           emptyDir, secret,\n902\t                                                           projected, pvc, …)\n903\t\n904\t   cumulative:  privileged  ⊃  baseline  ⊃  restricted\n905\t                (restricted includes every baseline requirement,\n906\t                 plus the rows below the line)\n907\t\n908\t\n909\t   THE MODES — what happens when a check fails\n910\t   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n911\t\n912\t           enforce  ──▶  the Pod is REJECTED\n913\t           audit    ──▶  recorded in the audit log; the Pod runs\n914\t           warn     ──▶  user-facing warning; the Pod runs\n915\t\n916\t\n917\t   APPLIED PER NAMESPACE, BY LABEL\n918\t   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n919\t\n920\t           pod-security.kubernetes.io/<MODE>: <LEVEL>\n921\t\n922\t   e.g.    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: baseline\n923\t           pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn:    restricted\n924\t           pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit:   restricted\n925\t\n926\t           ▲ all three, on one namespace, at two different levels.\n927\t             This is not a contradiction. It is a migration.\n928\t```\n929\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7de6482-238e-46bc-bfd1-6b5d0d0774fe","uuid":"29b2df5b-2f05-454e-bdbb-12a1da699a3c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:23:57.585Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-12\\draft-v1.md","content":"<!-- FIGURE: ch12-fig04-pod-security-standards-levels -->\n```\n   THE LEVELS — what gets checked\n   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n   securityContext field          privileged   baseline    restricted\n   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   privileged: true               allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n   hostNetwork/hostPID/hostIPC    allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n   hostPath volumes               allowed      ✗ forbidden ✗ forbidden\n   hostPort                       allowed      restricted  restricted\n   capabilities.add               allowed      known list  only\n                                                           NET_BIND_SERVICE\n   capabilities.drop              —            —           must include ALL\n   seccompProfile.type            allowed      not          RuntimeDefault\n                                               Unconfined   or Localhost\n   appArmorProfile.type           allowed      Runtime      Runtime\n                                               Default or   Default or\n                                               Localhost    Localhost\n   allowPrivilegeEscalation       allowed      —           must be false\n   runAsNonRoot                   —            —           must be true\n   runAsUser                      any          any         must be non-zero\n                                                           or unset\n   volume types                   any          any         safe list only\n                                                           (configMap, csi,\n                                                           emptyDir, secret,\n                                                           projected, pvc, …)\n\n   cumulative:  privileged  ⊃  baseline  ⊃  restricted\n                (restricted includes every baseline requirement,\n                 plus the rows below the line)\n\n\n   THE MODES — what happens when a check fails\n   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n           enforce  ──▶  the Pod is REJECTED\n           audit    ──▶  recorded in the audit log; the Pod runs\n           warn     ──▶  user-facing warning; the Pod runs\n\n\n   APPLIED PER NAMESPACE, BY LABEL\n   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n           pod-security.kubernetes.io/<MODE>: <LEVEL>\n\n   e.g.    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: baseline\n           pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn:    restricted\n           pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit:   restricted\n\n           ▲ all three, on one namespace, at two different levels.\n             This is not a contradiction. It is a migration.\n```\n","numLines":54,"startLine":876,"totalLines":1764}}}
